#26: 
hide_pid and pid_gid are proc mount options whose values are stored in the pid_namespace struct. As a result, if one mounts proc again for the same PID namespace with different mount options, all mounts for that PID namespace will be affected. This seems undesirable. This patch creates a proc_sb_info struct that points to the applicable PID namespace, and it moves hide_pid, pid_gid, and proc_self from pid_namespace to proc_sb_info. This patch removes a redundant null pointer check prior to calling dput which it would otherwise have to readd.

